<BaseLayout title="About — Layor76" description="Layor76 — gig driver who writes and records, Northeast Ohio.">
  <section class="px-6 py-12 lg:px-16 lg:py-16 max-w-2xl">
    <h1 class="font-display uppercase text-3xl sm:text-4xl text-ledger-paper mb-8">About</h1>
    <div class="text-steel leading-relaxed space-y-4 max-w-[62ch]">
      <p>
        Layor76 is a musician on Royal Legacy Records, based in Northeast Ohio. Also a 1099 gig
        driver — that's where the tax writing comes from, not a research hobby.
      </p>
      <p>
        Oldest of five, raised in Warren, Ohio, in a house with more struggle than stability.
        Worked young, worked a lot, learned early what it means to carry weight that isn't yours
        to carry. That's the throughline between the driving, the writing, and the record.
      </p>
      <p>
        The music is made for people who've lived through things they don't always know how to
        explain — childhood trauma, addiction, family pain, love, recovery, grief, and the fight
        to become something better than what tried to break you.
      </p>
      <p>
        He carries the same story on his skin — a left-forearm piece he designed himself, split
        between fire and ice. Survivor of the storm on one side, tempered by it on the other.
        <em class="not-italic">"I am not what broke me"</em> isn't a line he borrowed from
        anywhere — it's the whole idea, worn where he sees it every day.
      </p>
